     hhccsseeccdd..ccoonnff — hcsecd(8) configuration file

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The hhccsseeccdd..ccoonnff file is the configuration file for the hcsecd(8) Blue‐
     tooth link keys/PIN codes management daemon.

     The hhccsseeccdd..ccoonnff file is a free-form ASCII text file.  It is parsed by the
     recursive-descent parser built into hcsecd(8).  The file may contain ex‐
     tra tabs and newlines for formatting purposes.  Keywords in the file are
     case-sensitive.  Comments may be placed anywhere within the file (except
     within quotes).  Comments begin with the ‘#’ character and end at the end
     of the line.

FFIILLEE FFOORRMMAATT
     The hhccsseeccdd..ccoonnff file consists of a list of ddeevviiccee entries.  Each ddeevviiccee
     entry defines a link key or PIN code for a remote Bluetooth device.  Each
     remote Bluetooth device is identified by its unique BD_ADDR.

     The ddeevviiccee entry

     ddeevviiccee { ooppttiioonn _a_r_g_u_m_e_n_t; [ooppttiioonn _a_r_g_u_m_e_n_t;] }

     The following section describes all supported options and arguments.

     bbddaaddddrr _B_D___A_D_D_R
             Specify remote device BD_ADDR for the entry.

     nnaammee _d_e_v_i_c_e___n_a_m_e
             Specify user friendly name for the entry.  Name is a string in
             straight double quotes.

     kkeeyy _l_i_n_k___k_e_y
             Specify link key for the entry.  Link key is hexadecimal string
             up to 32 characters in length starting with ‘0x’.

     kkeeyy nnookkeeyy
             Specify no link key for the entry.

     ppiinn _P_I_N___c_o_d_e
             Specify PIN code for the entry.  PIN code is a string up to 16
             characters in length in straight double quotes.

     ppiinn nnooppiinn
             Specify no PIN code for the entry.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     A sample hhccsseeccdd..ccoonnff file:

     # Default entry is applied if no better match found
     # It MUST have 00:00:00:00:00:00 as bdaddr
     device {
             bdaddr  00:00:00:00:00:00;
             name    "Default entry";
             key     nokey;
             pin     nopin;
     }

     # Ericsson T68 phone
     device {
             bdaddr  00:80:37:5e:4d:d4;
             name    "Ericsson T68 phone";
             key     nokey;
             pin     "0000"; # PIN code
     }

     # Dummy device
     device {
             bdaddr  00:11:22:33:44:55;
             name    "Dummy";
             key     0x00112233445566778899aabbccddeeff; # 16 bytes key
             pin     nopin;
     }

